{%- comment -%}
  States the entrant's chance of winning, as a "1 in N" figure.

  Why this exists: a capped competition is one of the few prize formats where
  the odds are genuinely knowable, and publishing them is the strongest honest
  trust signal available. Competitors overwhelmingly do not.

  Why it is calculated against the published cap rather than entries sold:
  quoting the sold figure would flatter the number — with 2,570 of 4,000 taken,
  one entry reads as 1 in 2,570 instead of 1 in 4,000 — and it would drift every
  time somebody entered. The cap is fixed, published up front, and produces the
  *worst case* for the entrant. If the draw is made from sold entries only, a
  real chance can only be better than the figure shown. Understating is the only
  safe direction to be wrong in.

  It is off by default (settings.show_odds). The wording asserts how the draw
  pool is defined, so it must not appear until the competition rules say the
  same thing. docs/COMPETITION-DATA-MODEL.md covers what to confirm first.

  Parameters:
    product  (required)
    entries  entries being considered (default 1)
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign total = product.metafields.custom.entries_total.value
  assign held = entries | default: 1 | plus: 0

  assign can_show = false
  if settings.show_odds
    if total != blank and total > 0 and held > 0
      assign can_show = true
    endif
  endif

  comment
    More entries held than the cap is a data error, not a certainty of winning.
    Say nothing rather than claim "1 in 1".
  endcomment
  if held > total
    assign can_show = false
  endif
-%}

{%- if can_show -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign chance = total | divided_by: held
  -%}
  {%- capture chance_text -%}{%- render 'format-number', value: chance -%}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- assign chance_text = chance_text | strip -%}
  <p class="competition-odds">
    <span class="competition-odds__figure num">
      {{- 'products.competition.odds_value' | t: chance: chance_text -}}
    </span>
    <span class="competition-odds__note">{{ 'products.competition.odds_note' | t }}</span>
  </p>
{%- endif -%}
